# Official Building Blocks and Playbooks (catalog JSON)

Use this when adding or updating **official** hub listings (`is_official`, owner `openquok`) without a new `backend/supabase/db/listings/*_seed*.sql` migration in the same PR.

| Hub | `listing_kind` | Catalog file | Backfill (repo root) |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Building Blocks | `extension` | `backend/scripts/backfill_listings_building_blocks.catalog.json` | `pnpm backend:db:backfill-listings-building-blocks` |
| Playbooks | `stack` | `backend/scripts/backfill_listings_playbooks.catalog.json` | `pnpm backend:db:backfill-listings-playbooks` |

Production: append `:prod` to the script name. Always dry-run first: `-- --dry-run --slug <slug>`.

## Contributor checklist

1. Add `entries.<slug>` with a **stable UUID** on `listing.id`, explicit `listing.slug`, `category_slug`, `tag_slugs`, and editorial fields (snake_case aligned with `backend/data/schemas/listingSchemas.ts` / secret-admin).
2. Playbooks: set `stack_members[]` with `member_listing_slug`, `member_role`, `sort_order`. **Backfill building blocks before playbooks** when members are new.
3. Run local backfill after `supabase db reset` (catalog-only rows are not re-inserted by migrations alone).
4. Operator doc: `web/src/content/docs/admin/listings-catalog-backfill.md`.

## Do not

- Rely on secret-admin create for stable slugs — API derives slug from title; JSON backfill writes `slug` explicitly.
- Ship playbook members before member extension rows exist.
- Reset engagement counters — the backfill omits counter columns on update.
- Expect API cache purge — document ~5 minute TTL (same as link-directory catalog backfill).

## Prod → repo sync (optional)

`pnpm sync:listings-building-blocks-catalog-from-prod` or `pnpm sync:listings-playbooks-catalog-from-prod` merges production rows into catalog JSON; slugs in `PRESERVE_FROM_LOCAL` inside `sync_listings_catalog_from_prod.mjs` keep hand-curated repo copy.